"""How `{{ app_name }}` is READ. Nothing here ever writes (house rule 12).

Every function is `get_` or `list_` (house rule 16) and hands back a queryset
or a row, scoped both ways:

    def list_things(*, tenant: Tenant, org: Organization | None) -> ScopedQuerySet[Thing]:
        return (
            Thing.objects.for_tenant(tenant)
            .visible_to(org)
            .select_related("owner")
            .order_by("-created_at")
        )

`for_tenant` answers "whose data" and `visible_to` "which part of their
network". Both fail closed — an unresolved tenant or an unresolved hat reads an
empty table rather than the table — and on an org-scoped model the second half
is NOT optional (house rule 24).

A list route pins its query count at seeded scale (house rule 5), so the
`select_related` / `prefetch_related` that keeps it flat belongs here, where
every door inherits it.
"""

from __future__ import annotations
